<title>BELGIUM: GIB to invest 7 bln Bfr in 1997.</title>
<headline>GIB to invest 7 bln Bfr in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian retail group GIB SA plans to invest seven billion francs in 1997 on restructuring and development, it said in its 1996 annual report on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The funds will be used partly to strengthen its commercial agreement with France's Promodes and consolidate the recovery of Florida-based DIY chain Scotty's.</p>
<p>It will also be used to develop European DIY activities and continue the expansion and improve competitiveness of its Quick hamburger restaurant network.</p>
<p>GIB invested a total 5.9 billion francs in 1996.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
